IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2020(e), paragraphs (1) to (13): what the State plan of operation must provide.
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively). Same reading of results as snap4-s2020-a-d.l4: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING.
-- The text is the converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.


§ `s 2020(e) Requisites of State plan of operation`

-- src:1464 | The State plan of operation required under subsection (d) of this section shall provide, among such other provisions as may be required by regulation—
-- jural: the Secretary | each State agency | claim and duty: the plan provides the listed requisites and whatever regulation adds
@ref s 2020(e) (src:1464)
GIVEN `the requisite is listed in paragraphs (1) to (26) of subsection (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e) the State plan of operation must provide for the requisite` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requisite is listed in paragraphs (1) to (26) of subsection (e)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "among such other provisions as may be required by regulation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1465 | (1) that the State agency shall—
-- src:1466 | (A) at the option of the State agency, inform low-income households about the availability, eligibility requirements, application procedures, and benefits of the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
-- jural: low-income households | the State agency | none: an option of the State agency, not a duty owed to them unless it opts
@ref s 2020(e)(1)(A) (src:1465-1466)
GIVEN `the State agency has opted to inform low-income households` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(1)(A) the State agency must inform low-income households about the availability, eligibility requirements, application procedures and benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has opted to inform low-income households` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the option of the State agency, inform low-income households"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1467 | (B) comply with regulations of the Secretary requiring the use of appropriate bilingual personnel and printed material in the administration of the program in those portions of political subdivisions in the State in which a substantial number of members of low-income households speak a language other than English;
-- jural: members of low-income households who speak a language other than English | the State agency | claim and duty: bilingual personnel and printed material
@ref s 2020(e)(1)(B) (src:1467)
GIVEN `the portion of the political subdivision is one in which a substantial number of members of low-income households speak a language other than English` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(1)(B) the State agency must comply with the Secretary's regulations on bilingual personnel and printed material` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the portion of the political subdivision is one in which a substantial number of members of low-income households speak a language other than English` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in those portions of political subdivisions in the State in which a substantial number of members of low-income households speak a language other than English"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(e)(2)(A) household with special needs` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(e)(2)(A) a household with elderly or disabled members`
    `s 2020(e)(2)(A) a household in a rural area with low-income members`
    `s 2020(e)(2)(A) a homeless individual`
    `s 2020(e)(2)(A) a household residing on a reservation`
    `s 2020(e)(2)(A) a household in an area in which a substantial number of members of low-income households speak a language other than English`
    `s 2020(e)(2)(A) any other household`

-- src:1469 | (A) that the State agency shall establish procedures governing the operation of supplemental nutrition assistance program offices that the State agency determines best serve households in the State, including households with special needs, such as households with elderly or disabled members, households in rural areas with low-income members, homeless individuals, households residing on reservations, and households in areas in which a substantial number of members of low-income households speak a language other than English.
-- jural: households with special needs | the State agency | claim and duty: office procedures that best serve them, as the State agency determines
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(A) (src:1469)
GIVEN `the household` IS A `s 2020(e)(2)(A) household with special needs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(A) the State agency's office procedures must serve the household` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the household`
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(2)(A) any other household` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "including households with special needs, such as"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1470 | (B) In carrying out subparagraph (A), a State agency—
-- src:1471 | (i) shall provide timely, accurate, and fair service to applicants for, and participants in, the supplemental nutrition assistance program;
-- jural: applicants for, and participants in, the program | the State agency | claim and duty: timely, accurate and fair service
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(i) (src:1470-1471)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant for, or a participant in, the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(i) the State agency must provide the person with timely, accurate and fair service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an applicant for, or a participant in, the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "service to applicants for, and participants in, the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1472 | (ii)
-- src:1473 | (I) shall develop an application containing the information necessary to comply with this chapter; and
-- jural: applicants | the State agency | claim and duty: an application containing the information necessary to comply with this chapter
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(ii)(I) (src:1472-1473)
GIVEN `the information is necessary to comply with this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(ii)(I) the State agency's application must contain the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is necessary to comply with this chapter` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application containing the information necessary to comply with this chapter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1474 | (II) if the State agency maintains a website for the State agency, shall make the application available on the website in each language in which the State agency makes a printed application available;
-- jural: applicants who read the State agency's website | the State agency | claim and duty: the application on the website in each language in which a printed one is available
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(ii)(II) (src:1474)
GIVEN `the State agency maintains a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency makes a printed application available in the language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(ii)(II) the State agency must make the application available on its website in the language` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State agency maintains a website`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the State agency maintains a website for the State agency, shall make the application available on the website"
        IF `the State agency makes a printed application available in the language` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in each language in which the State agency makes a printed application available"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1475 | (iii) shall permit an applicant household to apply to participate in the program on the same day that the household first contacts a supplemental nutrition assistance program office in person during office hours;
-- jural: an applicant household | the State agency | claim and duty: the right to apply on the day of first in-person contact during office hours
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii) (src:1475)
GIVEN `the household first contacts a supplemental nutrition assistance program office in person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contact is during office hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iii) the State agency must permit the household to apply on the same day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household first contacts a supplemental nutrition assistance program office in person` AND `the contact is during office hours` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the same day that the household first contacts a supplemental nutrition assistance program office in person during office hours"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1476 | (iv) shall consider an application that contains the name, address, and signature of the applicant to be filed on the date the applicant submits the application;
-- jural: an applicant | the State agency | claim and duty: the application is filed on the day it is submitted
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv) (src:1476)
GIVEN `the application contains the name of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains the address of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains the signature of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the applicant submits the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(iv) the date on which the application is considered filed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application contains the name of the applicant` AND `the application contains the address of the applicant` AND `the application contains the signature of the applicant`
            THEN JUST `the date the applicant submits the application`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application that contains the name, address, and signature of the applicant"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1477 | (v) shall require that an adult representative of each applicant household certify in writing, under penalty of perjury, that—
-- src:1478 | (I) the information contained in the application is true; and
-- src:1479 | (II) all members of the household are citizens or are aliens eligible to receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits under section 2015(f) of this title;
-- jural: the State agency | an adult representative of each applicant household | claim and duty: a written certification under penalty of perjury
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(v) (src:1477-1479)
GIVEN `an adult representative of the household has certified in writing, under penalty of perjury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification says that the information contained in the application is true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certification says that all members of the household are citizens or are aliens eligible to receive benefits under section 2015(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(v) the certification required of the applicant household is complete` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an adult representative of the household has certified in writing, under penalty of perjury`
            AND `the certification says that the information contained in the application is true`
            AND `the certification says that all members of the household are citizens or are aliens eligible to receive benefits under section 2015(f)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states what the State agency shall require and not what follows from a certification missing one element
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1480 | (vi) shall provide a method of certifying and issuing benefits to eligible homeless individuals, to ensure that participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program is limited to eligible households; and
-- jural: eligible homeless individuals | the State agency | claim and duty: a method of certifying and issuing benefits
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(vi) (src:1480)
GIVEN `s 2012(l) the individual is a homeless individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(vi) the State agency must provide a method of certifying and issuing benefits to the individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2012(l) the individual is a homeless individual`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the individual is homeless is answered by section 2012(l)
    WHEN JUST homeless THEN
        BRANCH
            IF homeless AND `the individual is eligible` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to eligible homeless individuals"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1481 | (vii) may establish operating procedures that vary for local supplemental nutrition assistance program offices to reflect regional and local differences within the State.
-- jural: the State agency | local offices | privilege: procedures may vary to reflect regional and local differences
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(B)(vii) (src:1481)
GIVEN `the variation reflects regional and local differences within the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(B)(vii) the State agency may establish operating procedures that vary between local offices` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the variation reflects regional and local differences within the State` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to reflect regional and local differences within the State"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- inert: 1482 | reason 1 | the paragraph heading "Electronic and automated systems"
-- src:1483 | (i) In general.—
-- src:1484 | Nothing in this chapter shall prohibit the use of signatures provided and maintained electronically, storage of records using automated retrieval systems only, or any other feature of a State agency’s application system that does not rely exclusively on the collection and retention of paper applications or other records.
-- jural: the State agency | everyone | immunity: nothing in the chapter prohibits an electronic or automated feature
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(C)(i) (src:1483-1484)
GIVEN `the feature is an electronically provided and maintained signature, storage of records using automated retrieval systems only, or another feature of the application system that does not rely exclusively on paper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(C)(i) this chapter prohibits the feature` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the feature is an electronically provided and maintained signature, storage of records using automated retrieval systems only, or another feature of the application system that does not rely exclusively on paper`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this chapter shall prohibit the use of signatures provided and maintained electronically"
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks only of features that do not rely exclusively on paper
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1485 | (ii) State option for telephonic signature.—
-- src:1486 | A State agency may establish a system by which an applicant household may sign an application through a recorded verbal assent over the telephone.
-- jural: the State agency | an applicant household | power and liability: a State option to take a signature by recorded verbal assent over the telephone
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(C)(ii) (src:1485-1486)
GIVEN `the system lets an applicant household sign an application through a recorded verbal assent over the telephone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(C)(ii) the State agency may establish the system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the system lets an applicant household sign an application through a recorded verbal assent over the telephone` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text grants the option for this system only
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(e)(2)(C)(iii) facts about a telephonic signature system` HAS
    `(I) it records for future reference the verbal assent and the information to which assent was given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(II) it includes effective safeguards against impersonation, identity theft, and invasions of privacy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(III) it does not deny or interfere with the right of the household to apply in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(IV) it promptly provides the household member a written copy of the completed application, with instructions for correcting errors or omissions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(V) it complies with paragraph (1)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(VI) it satisfies all requirements for a signature on an application, with the date of verbal assent considered the date of application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `(VII) it complies with such other standards as the Secretary may establish` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1487 | (iii) Requirements.—
-- src:1488 | A system established under clause (ii) shall—
-- src:1489 | (I) record for future reference the verbal assent of the household member and the information to which assent was given;
-- src:1490 | (II) include effective safeguards against impersonation, identity theft, and invasions of privacy;
-- src:1491 | (III) not deny or interfere with the right of the household to apply in writing;
-- src:1492 | (IV) promptly provide to the household member a written copy of the completed application, with instructions for a simple procedure for correcting any errors or omissions;
-- src:1493 | (V) comply with paragraph (1)(B);
-- src:1494 | (VI) satisfy all requirements for a signature on an application under this chapter and other laws applicable to the supplemental nutrition assistance program, with the date on which the household member provides verbal assent considered as the date of application for all purposes; and
-- src:1495 | (VII) comply with such other standards as the Secretary may establish.
-- jural: the household | the State agency | claim and duty: the telephonic system must have the seven safeguards
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(C)(iii) (src:1487-1495)
GIVEN `the system` IS A `s 2020(e)(2)(C)(iii) facts about a telephonic signature system`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(C)(iii) the system meets the requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the system`'s `(I) it records for future reference the verbal assent and the information to which assent was given`
            AND `the system`'s `(II) it includes effective safeguards against impersonation, identity theft, and invasions of privacy`
            AND `the system`'s `(III) it does not deny or interfere with the right of the household to apply in writing`
            AND `the system`'s `(IV) it promptly provides the household member a written copy of the completed application, with instructions for correcting errors or omissions`
            AND `the system`'s `(V) it complies with paragraph (1)(B)`
            AND `the system`'s `(VI) it satisfies all requirements for a signature on an application, with the date of verbal assent considered the date of application`
            AND `the system`'s `(VII) it complies with such other standards as the Secretary may establish` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "A system established under clause (ii) shall" meet seven requirements and the text states no consequence for a system that misses one
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1494 | (VI) satisfy all requirements for a signature on an application under this chapter and other laws applicable to the supplemental nutrition assistance program, with the date on which the household member provides verbal assent considered as the date of application for all purposes; and
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(C)(iii)(VI) (src:1494)
GIVEN `the date on which the household member provides verbal assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2020(e)(2)(C)(iii)(VI) the date of application for all purposes` MEANS `the date on which the household member provides verbal assent`

-- src:1496 | (D) The signature of any adult under this paragraph shall be considered sufficient to comply with any provision of Federal law requiring a household member to sign an application or statement;
-- jural: any adult household member | Federal law requiring a signature | power: one adult's signature suffices
@ref s 2020(e)(2)(D) (src:1496)
GIVEN `the signer is an adult` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(2)(D) the signature is sufficient to comply with a provision of Federal law requiring a household member to sign an application or statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the signer is an adult` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The signature of any adult under this paragraph"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(e)(3) factor to be verified` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(e)(3) income not excluded by section 2014(d)`
    `s 2020(e)(3) income excluded by section 2014(d)`
    `s 2020(e)(3) household size where the size is questionable`
    `s 2020(e)(3) household size where the size is not questionable`
    `s 2020(e)(3) another eligibility factor the Secretary determines necessary to implement sections 2014 and 2015`
    `s 2020(e)(3) another eligibility factor the State agency determines necessary`

DECLARE `s 2020(e) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(e)(3) complete certification and provide the allotment`
    `s 2020(e)(9) provide benefits`

-- src:1497 | that the State agency shall thereafter promptly determine the eligibility of each applicant household by way of verification of income other than that determined to be excluded by section 2014(d) of this title (in part through the use of the information, if any, obtained under section 2025(e) of this title and after compliance with the requirement specified in paragraph (24)), household size (in any case such size is questionable), and such other eligibility factors as the Secretary determines to be necessary to implement sections 2014 and 2015 of this title, …
-- jural: the State agency | applicant households | power and liability: income, questionable household size and the Secretary's other factors are verified
@ref s 2020(e)(3) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the factor` IS A `s 2020(e)(3) factor to be verified`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(3) the State agency must verify the factor before determining eligibility` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the factor`
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) income not excluded by section 2014(d)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) income excluded by section 2014(d)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "verification of income other than that determined to be excluded by section 2014(d)"
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) household size where the size is questionable` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) household size where the size is not questionable` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "household size (in any case such size is questionable)"
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) another eligibility factor the Secretary determines necessary to implement sections 2014 and 2015` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) another eligibility factor the State agency determines necessary` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): this factor is the State agency's option in the next clause, not a duty here

-- src:1497 | although the State agency may verify prior to certification, whether questionable or not, the size of any applicant household and such other eligibility factors as the State agency determines are necessary, …
-- jural: the State agency | applicant households | privilege and no-right: verification before certification, questionable or not
@ref s 2020(e)(3) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the factor` IS A `s 2020(e)(3) factor to be verified`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(3) the State agency may verify the factor prior to certification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the factor`
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) household size where the size is questionable` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) household size where the size is not questionable` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(3) another eligibility factor the State agency determines necessary` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the option names the size of a household and the factors the State agency determines necessary, and nothing else
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1497 | so as to complete certification of and provide an allotment retroactive to the period of application to any eligible household not later than thirty days following its filing of an application, …
-- jural: an eligible household | the State agency | claim and duty: certification and an allotment retroactive to the period of application, within thirty days of filing
@ref s 2020(e)(3) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the household is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(3) the household is entitled to certification and a retroactive allotment within thirty days of filing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is eligible` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any eligible household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2020(e)(3) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the date the household filed its application` IS A DATE
      `the date the State agency completed certification and provided the allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test (thirty days), not a ruling: TRUE on the thirtieth day, FALSE on the thirty-first.
`s 2020(e)(3) certification and the allotment were completed not later than thirty days following filing` MEANS
    `the date the State agency completed certification and provided the allotment` AT MOST (`the date the household filed its application` PLUS 30)

-- The duty as a regulative rule: 30 is a number of days on the file's clock.
@ref s 2020(e)(3) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the household is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 2020(e) act`
`s 2020(e)(3) the thirty-day duty` MEANS
    IF `the household is eligible`
    THEN PARTY `the State agency`
         MUST `s 2020(e)(3) complete certification and provide the allotment`
         WITHIN 30
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "certification and the allotment were not completed within thirty days of filing the application"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1497 | and that the State agency shall provide each applicant household, at the time of application, a clear written statement explaining what acts the household must perform to cooperate in obtaining verification and otherwise completing the application process;
-- jural: each applicant household | the State agency | claim and duty: a clear written statement of what it must do to cooperate, at the time of application
@ref s 2020(e)(3) (src:1497)
GIVEN `the household is an applicant household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the time of application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(3) the State agency must give the household a clear written statement of what it must do to cooperate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is an applicant household` AND `it is the time of application` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each applicant household, at the time of application"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1498 | that the State agency shall insure that each participating household receive a notice of expiration of its certification prior to the start of the last month of its certification period advising the household that it must submit a new application in order to renew its eligibility for a new certification period …
-- jural: each participating household | the State agency | claim and duty: a notice of expiration before the last month of the certification period
@ref s 2020(e)(4) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the day the last month of the certification period starts` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of expiration was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test: the notice must go "prior to the start of the last month", so the day the last month starts is too late.
`s 2020(e)(4) the notice of expiration was sent prior to the start of the last month of the certification period` MEANS
    `the day the notice of expiration was sent` LESS THAN `the day the last month of the certification period starts`

-- src:1498 | each such household which seeks to be certified another time or more times thereafter by filing an application for such recertification no later than fifteen days prior to the day upon which its existing certification period expires …
@ref s 2020(e)(4) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the day the existing certification period expires` IS A DATE
      `the day the household filed its application for recertification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test: filed "no later than fifteen days prior to the day upon which its existing certification period expires".
`s 2020(e)(4) the application for recertification was filed no later than fifteen days prior to the expiry` MEANS
    `the day the household filed its application for recertification` AT MOST (`the day the existing certification period expires` MINUS 15)

-- src:1498 | shall, if found to be still eligible, receive its allotment no later than one month after the receipt of the last allotment issued to it pursuant to its prior certification, …
-- jural: a household that recertifies in time | the State agency | claim and duty: the next allotment within one month of the last
@ref s 2020(e)(4) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the household was found to be still eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household filed its application for recertification in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(4) the household is entitled to its next allotment no later than one month after the last` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household filed its application for recertification in time` AND `the household was found to be still eligible` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each such household which seeks to be certified another time ... no later than fifteen days prior ... shall, if found to be still eligible"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2020(e)(4) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the day the household received the last allotment issued under its prior certification` IS A DATE
      `the day the household received the next allotment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test: one calendar month (the month arithmetic of the daydate library), not thirty days.
`s 2020(e)(4) the next allotment was received no later than one month after the last` MEANS
    `the day the household received the next allotment` AT MOST (`add months` `the day the household received the last allotment issued under its prior certification` 1)

-- src:1498 | but if such household is found to be ineligible or to be eligible for a smaller allotment during the new certification period it shall not continue to participate and receive benefits on the basis authorized for the preceding certification period even if it makes a timely request for a fair hearing pursuant to paragraph (10) of this subsection: …
-- jural: the State agency | a household found ineligible or eligible for a smaller allotment | immunity of the agency against the hearing request: the household does not continue on the old basis
@ref s 2020(e)(4) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the household is found ineligible, or eligible for a smaller allotment, during the new certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(4) the household continues to receive benefits on the basis of the preceding certification period pending a fair hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is found ineligible, or eligible for a smaller allotment, during the new certification period`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall not continue to participate and receive benefits on the basis authorized for the preceding certification period even if it makes a timely request for a fair hearing"
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if such household is found to be ineligible or to be eligible for a smaller allotment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1498 | Provided, That the timeliness standards for submitting the notice of expiration and filing an application for recertification may be modified by the Secretary in light of sections 2014(f)(2) and 2015(c) of this title if administratively necessary;
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency and the household | power and liability: the timeliness standards may be modified
@ref s 2020(e)(4) (src:1498)
GIVEN `the modification is administratively necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(4) the Secretary may modify the timeliness standards` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the modification is administratively necessary` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be modified by the Secretary in light of sections 2014(f)(2) and 2015(c) of this title if administratively necessary"

-- src:1499 | (5) the specific standards to be used in determining the eligibility of applicant households which shall be in accordance with sections 2014 and 2015 of this title and shall include no additional requirements imposed by the State agency;
-- jural: an applicant household | the State agency | immunity: the State agency may add no eligibility requirement to sections 2014 and 2015
@ref s 2020(e)(5) (src:1499)
GIVEN `the requirement is additional to those in sections 2014 and 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(5) the State agency may impose the requirement in determining eligibility` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirement is additional to those in sections 2014 and 2015`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall include no additional requirements imposed by the State agency"
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a requirement that is in sections 2014 and 2015 is not spoken of here
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1500 | (6) that—
-- src:1501 | (A) the State agency shall undertake the certification of applicant households in accordance with the general procedures prescribed by the Secretary in the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter; and
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | claim and duty: certification follows the Secretary's general procedures
@ref s 2020(e)(6)(A) (src:1500-1501)
GIVEN `the procedure is a general procedure prescribed by the Secretary in the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(6)(A) the State agency must undertake certification in accordance with the procedure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the procedure is a general procedure prescribed by the Secretary in the regulations issued pursuant to this chapter` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the general procedures prescribed by the Secretary in the regulations"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1502 | (B) the State agency personnel utilized in undertaking such certification shall be employed in accordance with the current standards for a Merit System of Personnel Administration or any standards later prescribed by the Office of Personnel Management pursuant to section 4728 of title 42 modifying or superseding such standards relating to the establishment and maintenance of personnel standards on a merit basis;
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | claim and duty: certifying personnel are employed on merit-system standards
@ref s 2020(e)(6)(B) (src:1502)
GIVEN `the person is State agency personnel utilized in undertaking certification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(6)(B) the State agency must employ the person in accordance with merit system standards` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is State agency personnel utilized in undertaking certification` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the State agency personnel utilized in undertaking such certification"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(e)(7) purpose of the representation` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(e)(7) the certification process`
    `s 2020(e)(7) benefit issuance`
    `s 2020(e)(7) food purchase`

-- src:1503 | (7) that an applicant household may be represented in the certification process and that an eligible household may be represented in benefit issuance or food purchase by a person other than a member of the household so long as that person has been clearly designated as the representative of that household for that purpose by the head of the household or the spouse of the head, and, where the certification process is concerned, the representative is an adult who is sufficiently aware of relevant household circumstances, except that the Secretary may restrict the number of households which may be represented by an individual and otherwise establish criteria and verification standards for representation under this paragraph;
-- jural: an applicant or eligible household | the State agency | privilege and no-right: to be represented by a non-member clearly designated; the Secretary may restrict the number and set criteria
@ref s 2020(e)(7) (src:1503)
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 2020(e)(7) purpose of the representation`
      `the person is clearly designated as the representative of that household for that purpose by the head of the household or the spouse of the head` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an adult sufficiently aware of relevant household circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a restriction or criterion of the Secretary bars the representation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(7) the household may be represented by a person other than a member of the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is clearly designated as the representative of that household for that purpose by the head of the household or the spouse of the head`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as that person has been clearly designated as the representative of that household for that purpose"
        IF `the purpose` EQUALS `s 2020(e)(7) the certification process` AND (NOT `the person is an adult sufficiently aware of relevant household circumstances`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the certification process is concerned, the representative is an adult who is sufficiently aware of relevant household circumstances"
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the Secretary may restrict the number of households which may be represented by an individual and otherwise establish criteria and verification standards"
        IF `a restriction or criterion of the Secretary bars the representation` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 2020(e)(8) use or disclosure of information obtained from applicant households` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(e)(8)(A)(i) disclosure to persons directly connected with the administration or enforcement of this chapter, its regulations, Federal assistance programs, or federally-assisted State programs`
    `s 2020(e)(8)(A)(ii) subsequent use by those persons only for such administration or enforcement`
    `s 2020(e)(8)(B) use or disclosure to the Comptroller General of the United States for audit and examination`
    `s 2020(e)(8)(C) disclosure on request to local, State or Federal law enforcement officials to investigate an alleged violation of this chapter or a regulation under it`
    `s 2020(e)(8)(D) use or disclosure to Federal agencies to collect an overissuance from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund`
    `s 2020(e)(8)(E) disclosure of the address, social security number and photograph of a member to a law enforcement officer who has made the required notification`
    `s 2020(e)(8)(F) use or disclosure needed to comply with paragraph (15) or (18)(B) or subsection (u)`
    `s 2020(e)(8) any other use or disclosure`

-- src:1504 | (8) safeguards which prohibit the use or disclosure of information obtained from applicant households, except that—
-- src:1505 | (A) the safeguards shall permit—
-- src:1506 | (i) the disclosure of such information to persons directly connected with the administration or enforcement of the provisions of this chapter, regulations issued pursuant to this chapter, Federal assistance programs, or federally-assisted State programs; and
-- src:1507 | (ii) the subsequent use of the information by persons described in clause (i) only for such administration or enforcement;
-- src:1508 | (B) the safeguards shall not prevent the use or disclosure of such information to the Comptroller General of the United States for audit and examination authorized by any other provision of law;
-- src:1509 | (C) notwithstanding any other provision of law, all information obtained under this chapter from an applicant household shall be made available, upon request, to local, State or Federal law enforcement officials for the purpose of investigating an alleged violation of this chapter or any regulation issued under this chapter;
-- src:1510 | (D) the safeguards shall not prevent the use by, or disclosure of such information, to agencies of the Federal Government (including the United States Postal Service) for purposes of collecting the amount of an overissuance of benefits, as determined under section 2022(b) of this title, from Federal pay (including salaries and pensions) as authorized pursuant to section 5514 of title 5 or a Federal income tax refund as authorized by section 3720A of title 31;
-- src:1517 | (F) the safeguards shall not prevent compliance with paragraph (15) or (18)(B) or subsection (u);
-- jural: an applicant household | the State agency | immunity: information from the household is protected except for the listed uses
@ref s 2020(e)(8) (src:1504-1517)
GIVEN `the use or disclosure` IS A `s 2020(e)(8) use or disclosure of information obtained from applicant households`
      `the conditions the paragraph attaches to the use or disclosure are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(8) the safeguards must prohibit the use or disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the use or disclosure`
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(8) any other use or disclosure` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(8)(C) disclosure on request to local, State or Federal law enforcement officials to investigate an alleged violation of this chapter or a regulation under it` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that" lifts the prohibition for this use when its conditions are met, and only then
        IF `the conditions the paragraph attaches to the use or disclosure are met` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2020(e)(8)(E) disclosure of the address, social security number and photograph of a member to a law enforcement officer who has made the required notification` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except that" lifts the prohibition for this use when its conditions are met, and only then
        IF `the conditions the paragraph attaches to the use or disclosure are met` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "safeguards which prohibit the use or disclosure of information obtained from applicant households, except that" (the uses in (A)(i), (A)(ii), (B), (D) and (F) are the exceptions)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1509 | (C) notwithstanding any other provision of law, all information obtained under this chapter from an applicant household shall be made available, upon request, to local, State or Federal law enforcement officials for the purpose of investigating an alleged violation of this chapter or any regulation issued under this chapter;
@ref s 2020(e)(8)(C) (src:1509)
GIVEN `the request is made by a local, State or Federal law enforcement official` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to investigate an alleged violation of this chapter or a regulation under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(8)(C) the information obtained from an applicant household must be made available to the official` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the request is made by a local, State or Federal law enforcement official` AND `the purpose is to investigate an alleged violation of this chapter or a regulation under it` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon request, to local, State or Federal law enforcement officials for the purpose of investigating an alleged violation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(e)(8)(E) notification by a law enforcement officer` HAS
    `the officer is a Federal, State, or local law enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer furnishes the State agency with the name of the member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer notifies the agency that the member is fleeing to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a felony (or, in New Jersey, a high misdemeanor), or is violating a condition of probation or parole` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer notifies the agency that the member has information necessary for an official duty related to that` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer notifies the agency that locating or apprehending the member is an official duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer notifies the agency that the request is being made in the proper exercise of an official duty` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1511 | (E) notwithstanding any other provision of law, the address, social security number, and, if available, photograph of any member of a household shall be made available, on request, to any Federal, State, or local law enforcement officer if the officer furnishes the State agency with the name of the member and notifies the agency that—
-- src:1512 | (i) the member—
-- src:1513 | (I) is fleeing to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a crime (or attempt to commit a crime) that, under the law of the place the member is fleeing, is a felony (or, in the case of New Jersey, a high misdemeanor), or is violating a condition of probation or parole imposed under Federal or State law; or
-- src:1514 | (II) has information that is necessary for the officer to conduct an official duty related to subclause (I);
-- src:1515 | (ii) locating or apprehending the member is an official duty; and
-- src:1516 | (iii) the request is being made in the proper exercise of an official duty; and
-- jural: a law enforcement officer | the State agency | claim and duty: the address, social security number and photograph of a member on request
@ref s 2020(e)(8)(E) (src:1511-1516)
GIVEN `the officer` IS A `s 2020(e)(8)(E) notification by a law enforcement officer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(8)(E) the address, social security number and, if available, photograph of the member must be made available on request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the officer`'s `the officer is a Federal, State, or local law enforcement officer`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any Federal, State, or local law enforcement officer"
        IF `the officer`'s `the officer is a Federal, State, or local law enforcement officer`
            AND `the officer`'s `the officer furnishes the State agency with the name of the member`
            AND (`the officer`'s `the officer notifies the agency that the member is fleeing to avoid prosecution, or custody or confinement after conviction, for a felony (or, in New Jersey, a high misdemeanor), or is violating a condition of probation or parole`
                 OR `the officer`'s `the officer notifies the agency that the member has information necessary for an official duty related to that`)
            AND `the officer`'s `the officer notifies the agency that locating or apprehending the member is an official duty`
            AND `the officer`'s `the officer notifies the agency that the request is being made in the proper exercise of an official duty` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the officer furnishes the State agency with the name of the member and notifies the agency that"

-- src:1518 | (9) that the State agency shall—
-- src:1519 | (A) provide benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application to any household which—
-- src:1520 | (i)
-- src:1521 | (I) has gross income that is less than $150 per month; or
-- src:1522 | (II) is a destitute migrant or a seasonal farmworker household in accordance with the regulations governing such households in effect July 1, 1982; and
-- src:1523 | (ii) has liquid resources that do not exceed $100;
-- jural: a household with little income and few resources, or a destitute migrant or seasonal farmworker household | the State agency | claim and duty: benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application
@ref s 2020(e)(9)(A) (src:1518-1523)
GIVEN `the household's gross income per month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the household is a destitute migrant or a seasonal farmworker household in accordance with the regulations in effect July 1, 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household's liquid resources, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(9)(A) the household is entitled to benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the household's gross income per month, in dollars` LESS THAN 150 OR `the household is a destitute migrant or a seasonal farmworker household in accordance with the regulations in effect July 1, 1982`)
            AND `the household's liquid resources, in dollars` AT MOST 100 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any household which" ... "(I) has gross income that is less than $150 per month; or" ... "(II) is a destitute migrant or a seasonal farmworker household" ... "(ii) has liquid resources that do not exceed $100"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1524 | (B) provide benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application to any household that has a combined gross income and liquid resources that is less than the monthly rent, or mortgage, and utilities of the household; and
-- jural: a household whose income and resources are less than its rent or mortgage and utilities | the State agency | claim and duty: benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application
@ref s 2020(e)(9)(B) (src:1524)
GIVEN `the household's gross income per month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the household's liquid resources, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the household's monthly rent, or mortgage, and utilities, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(9)(B) the household is entitled to benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household's gross income per month, in dollars` PLUS `the household's liquid resources, in dollars` LESS THAN `the household's monthly rent, or mortgage, and utilities, in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any household that has a combined gross income and liquid resources that is less than the monthly rent, or mortgage, and utilities of the household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1519 | (A) provide benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application to any household which—
-- src:1524 | (B) provide benefits no later than 7 days after the date of application to any household that has a combined gross income and liquid resources that is less than the monthly rent, or mortgage, and utilities of the household; and
@ref s 2020(e)(9) (src:1519-1524)
GIVEN `the date of application` IS A DATE
      `the date the household received benefits` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- A period test (7 days): TRUE on the seventh day after the date of application, FALSE on the eighth.
`s 2020(e)(9) benefits were provided no later than 7 days after the date of application` MEANS
    `the date the household received benefits` AT MOST (`the date of application` PLUS 7)

@ref s 2020(e)(9) (src:1519-1524)
GIVEN `the household is entitled under paragraph (9)(A) or (9)(B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 2020(e) act`
`s 2020(e)(9) the seven-day duty` MEANS
    IF `the household is entitled under paragraph (9)(A) or (9)(B)`
    THEN PARTY `the State agency`
         MUST `s 2020(e)(9) provide benefits`
         WITHIN 7
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "benefits were not provided within 7 days after the date of application"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1525 | (C) to the extent practicable, verify the income and liquid resources of a household referred to in subparagraph (A) or (B) prior to issuance of benefits to the household;
-- jural: the State agency | a household referred to in (9)(A) or (9)(B) | power and liability: income and liquid resources are verified before issuance, to the extent practicable
@ref s 2020(e)(9)(C) (src:1525)
GIVEN `the household is one referred to in subparagraph (A) or (B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is practicable to verify before issuance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(9)(C) the State agency must verify the income and liquid resources prior to issuance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is one referred to in subparagraph (A) or (B)` AND `it is practicable to verify before issuance` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent practicable, verify the income and liquid resources of a household referred to in subparagraph (A) or (B)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1526 | for the granting of a fair hearing and a prompt determination thereafter to any household aggrieved by the action of the State agency under any provision of its plan of operation as it affects the participation of such household in the supplemental nutrition assistance program or by a claim against the household for an overissuance: …
-- jural: an aggrieved household | the State agency | claim and duty: a fair hearing and a prompt determination
@ref s 2020(e)(10) (src:1526)
GIVEN `the household is aggrieved by the action of the State agency under a provision of its plan of operation as it affects the participation of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is aggrieved by a claim against it for an overissuance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(10) the household is entitled to a fair hearing and a prompt determination thereafter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is aggrieved by the action of the State agency under a provision of its plan of operation as it affects the participation of the household`
            OR `the household is aggrieved by a claim against it for an overissuance` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any household aggrieved by the action of the State agency"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1526 | Provided, That any household which timely requests such a fair hearing after receiving individual notice of agency action reducing or terminating its benefits within the household’s certification period shall continue to participate and receive benefits on the basis authorized immediately prior to the notice of adverse action until such time as the fair hearing is completed and an adverse decision rendered or until such time as the household’s certification period terminates, whichever occurs earlier, …
-- jural: a household whose benefits are reduced or terminated within its certification period | the State agency | claim and duty: benefits continue on the old basis until the hearing is completed
@ref s 2020(e)(10) (src:1526)
GIVEN `the household timely requested a fair hearing after receiving individual notice of agency action reducing or terminating its benefits within the certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing has been completed and an adverse decision rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household's certification period has terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(10) the household continues to participate and receive benefits on the basis authorized immediately prior to the notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the household timely requested a fair hearing after receiving individual notice of agency action reducing or terminating its benefits within the certification period`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any household which timely requests such a fair hearing after receiving individual notice of agency action reducing or terminating its benefits within the household's certification period"
        IF `the hearing has been completed and an adverse decision rendered` OR `the household's certification period has terminated`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until such time as the fair hearing is completed and an adverse decision rendered or until such time as the household's certification period terminates"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1526 | except that in any case in which the State agency receives from the household a written statement containing information that clearly requires a reduction or termination of the household’s benefits, the State agency may act immediately to reduce or terminate the household’s benefits and may provide notice of its action to the household as late as the date on which the action becomes effective. …
-- jural: the State agency | the household | power and liability: immediate reduction or termination, with notice as late as the day the action takes effect
@ref s 2020(e)(10) (src:1526)
GIVEN `the State agency receives from the household a written statement containing information that clearly requires a reduction or termination of the household's benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(10) the State agency may act immediately and give notice as late as the date on which the action becomes effective` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency receives from the household a written statement containing information that clearly requires a reduction or termination of the household's benefits` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any case in which the State agency receives from the household a written statement containing information that clearly requires a reduction or termination"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1526 | At the option of a State, at any time prior to a fair hearing determination under this paragraph, a household may withdraw, orally or in writing, a request by the household for the fair hearing. If the withdrawal request is an oral request, the State agency shall provide a written notice to the household confirming the withdrawal request and providing the household with an opportunity to request a hearing;
-- jural: the household | the State agency | power and liability: withdrawal of the hearing request, orally or in writing; an oral withdrawal is confirmed in writing
@ref s 2020(e)(10) (src:1526)
GIVEN `the State has opted to allow withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a fair hearing determination has not yet been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the withdrawal is an oral request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(10) the State agency must provide a written notice confirming the withdrawal and an opportunity to request a hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State has opted to allow withdrawal` AND `a fair hearing determination has not yet been made` AND `the withdrawal is an oral request` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the option of a State, at any time prior to a fair hearing determination ... If the withdrawal request is an oral request"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1527 | upon receipt of a request from a household, for the prompt restoration in the form of benefits to a household of any allotment or portion thereof which has been wrongfully denied or terminated, except that allotments shall not be restored for any period of time more than one year prior to the date the State agency receives a request for such restoration from a household or the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers that a loss to a household has occurred;
-- jural: a household whose allotment was wrongfully denied or terminated | the State agency | claim and duty: prompt restoration in benefits, for not more than one year before the request or discovery
@ref s 2020(e)(11) (src:1527)
GIVEN `the household has requested restoration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment or portion of it was wrongfully denied or terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of the period for which restoration is sought` IS A DATE
      `the date the State agency first receives a request from the household, is notified, or otherwise discovers that a loss has occurred` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(e)(11) the period must be restored to the household in the form of benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first day of the period for which restoration is sought` LESS THAN (`add months` `the date the State agency first receives a request from the household, is notified, or otherwise discovers that a loss has occurred` (0 MINUS 12))
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "allotments shall not be restored for any period of time more than one year prior to the date the State agency receives a request for such restoration from a household or the State agency is notified or otherwise discovers that a loss to a household has occurred"
        IF `the household has requested restoration` AND `the allotment or portion of it was wrongfully denied or terminated` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon receipt of a request from a household, for the prompt restoration ... of any allotment or portion thereof which has been wrongfully denied or terminated"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

